NOTE: 

The examples in this directory are described in the userguide.

NOTE: Examples interface_tracking1e-interface_tracking6e are similar to
interface_tracking1-interface_tracking6, but use the explicit scheme.

Short description
-----------------

interface_tracking1

 Tracking of an initially circular interface in a flow given by a function.
 Interface moves in normal direction.
 SUPG with semi-implicit second-order time integration.
 tfem mesh made using mesh_skeleton.
 Error output.

interface_tracking2

 Tracking of an initially spherical interface in a flow given by a function.
 Interface moves in normal direction.
 SUPG with semi-implicit second-order time integration.
 Gmsh mesh with six-node triangles.
 Error output

interface_tracking3

 Tracking of an initially circular interface in a flow given by a function.
 Tangential grid deformation in addition to the movement in normal direction.
 SUPG with semi-implicit second-order time integration.
 tfem mesh made using mesh_skeleton.
 Tangential grid deformation.
 Error output

interface_tracking4

 Tracking of an initially spherical interface in a flow given by a function.
 Tangential grid deformation in addition to the movement in normal direction.
 SUPG with semi-implicit second-order time integration.
 Gmsh mesh with six-node triangles.
 Tangential grid deformation.
 Error output

interface_tracking5

 Tracking of an initially circular interface in a flow given by a function.
 Interface movement is Lagrange based.
 Tangential grid deformation.
 Second-order time integration (performed on element level).
 tfem mesh made using mesh_skeleton.
 Error output

interface_tracking6

 Tracking of an initially spherical interface in a flow given by a function.
 Interface movement is Lagrange based.
 Tangential grid deformation.
 Second-order time integration (performed on element level).
 Gmsh mesh with six-node triangles.
 Error output

interface_tracking7

 Tracking of an initially square interface in a flow given by a function.
 Interface moves in normal direction.
 SUPG with semi-implicit second-order time integration.
 tfem mesh made using mesh_skeleton.

interface_tracking8

 Tracking of an initially square interface in a flow given by a function.
 Interface movement is Lagrangian.
 Explicit second-order time integration (on element level).
 tfem mesh made using mesh_skeleton.

interface_tracking9

 Tracking of an initially circular interface in a flow given by a function.
 Interface movement is Lagrangian.
 No tangential grid deformation (u_t=0).
 Second-order time integration (performed on element level).
 tfem mesh made using mesh_skeleton.
 Error output
 Note: similar to interface_tracking5, but u_t=0.

interface_tracking10

 Tracking of an initially spherical interface in a flow given by a function.
 Interface movement is Lagrangian.
 No tangential grid deformation (u_t=0).
 Second-order time integration (performed on element level).
 Gmsh mesh with six-node triangles.
 Error output
 Note: similar to interface_tracking6, but u_t=0.

interface_tracking11

 Tracking of an initially circular interface in a flow given by a function.
 Only the upper half is solved using the full system with symmetry conditions.
 Therefore only elongational flow (vfuncnr=1) is applicable.
 Interface moves in normal direction.
 SUPG with semi-implicit second-order time integration.
 tfem mesh made using mesh_skeleton.
 Error output.
 Note: similar to interface_tracking1, but now solving only the upper half
       of the domain.

interface_tracking12

 Tracking of an initially circular interface in a flow given by a function.
 Only the upper half is solved using the full system with symmetry conditions.
 Therefore only elongational flow (vfuncnr=1) is applicable.
 Tangential grid deformation in addition to the movement in normal direction.
 SUPG with semi-implicit second-order time integration.
 tfem mesh made using mesh_skeleton.
 Error output
 Note: similar to interface_tracking3, but now solving only the upper half
       of the domain.

interface_tracking13

 Tracking of an initially circular interface in a flow given by a function.
 Interface movement is Lagrangian.
 No tangential grid deformation (u_t=0).
 Only the upper half is solved using the full system with symmetry conditions.
 Therefore only elongational flow (vfuncnr=1) is applicable.
 tfem mesh made using mesh_skeleton.
 Error output.
 Note: similar to interface_tracking9, but now solving only the upper half
       of the domain.

